Placed before `sessionUser`, it logs unauthenticated/401 requests too; the `req.user` check just degrades gracefully since auth hasn't run yet on that first pass. Log on `res.on("finish")` rather than at entry, so it captures the real status code, and rather than after the handler returns, so it also fires on the hung/unhandled-rejection case from the connection-drop scenario (never resolves) — actually it won't fire then either, since `finish` needs a response to be sent; note that as a limit, not a claim of coverage.

